## Run B: post-boot companion from the list
$ CV_PROJECT=fixtures/corpus-src/happy ./target/debug/cv-app --window-script /tmp/cv-probe/main2.json
  rune-script-window main
  rune-mark companion-requested 2.4 2.401
  rune-script-done 2.4 2.401

Script: tap "row-index.md", Enter.
CGWindowList at +3s:
  win=12792 main        bounds 1280x800 @ 260,109
  win=12800 companion   bounds  560x640 @ 620,149   <- reader companion opened mid-run

## Run C: palette "Close companion windows" retires it
$ CV_PROJECT=fixtures/corpus-src/happy ./target/debug/cv-app --window-script /tmp/cv-probe/main3.json
Script: tap row -> Enter (open), cmd+k -> type "close companion" -> Enter.
CGWindowList at +4s and +8s: main window only; companion opened at ~1.2s
was gone by +4s. rune-mark close-requested 4.4; script done, no errors.

## Gotchas
- Palette filter: typing "companion" alone can highlight
  "Close companion windows" instead of "Open selection in companion
  window" (run order matters); a first attempt no-opped that way.
- Scripted "ime"/"menu"/"shortcut" kinds do NOT replay on real windows
  (window_script step only lands canvas input: move/down/up/tap/drag,
  keys, wheel). IME still needs a real OS input method.
- No assistive access or screen recording on this host: no AppleScript
  keystrokes, no window titles (CGWindowList reports names only with
  Screen Recording), no screencapture. Dirty-close (native close button)
  and clean-quit-via-window-close remain OS-gesture-only here.
